          "heading": "Jake White emerges as leading candidate for Fiji head coach vacancy",
          "body": "Former Springboks boss Jake White has emerged as the leading candidate to become the next Fiji head coach ahead of the 2027 Rugby World Cup. The World Cup-winning coach joins a high-profile field of contenders as Fiji Rugby seeks a permanent successor to Mick Byrne, who departed by mutual agreement in April. With the coaching search intensified, White's pedigree makes him a prominent frontrunner to guide the national team out of their recent slump, following three successive defeats that have left them bottom of the standings."
