          "body": "The Ireland women's squad secured consecutive victories over Japan with a comprehensive 43-19 win at Virgin Media Park on Saturday. Scott Bemand's side scored seven tries, recovering from an early deficit to lead 22-7 at half-time. Brittany Hogan and Beibhinn Parsons both crossed the line, with Parsons extending her record to 25 international tries, while debutants Alana McInerney and Sophie Barrett scored after coming off the bench. The squad now travels to South Africa for their WXV campaign with significant momentum."
