          "body": "The Argentine Rugby Union has submitted its technical proposal to World Rugby, nominating eight domestic stadiums for the joint 2035 Rugby World Cup bid. Argentina is leading the four-nation project alongside Uruguay, Chile and Brazil, with famous venues like Buenos Aires' Estadio Monumental and Rio de Janeiro's Maracanã included. Union president Félix Páez Molina hailed the bid as a vital step, as the South American coalition prepares to compete against Japan and Spain before the hosting decision in November 2027."
